WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.611
BAML now compiles

00:00:01.423 --> 00:00:02.390
to Rust up

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.887
to 34x faster

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:05.447
Boundary wrote a

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:06.344
new backend for

00:00:06.155 --> 00:00:07.499
the BAML compiler

00:00:07.323 --> 00:00:08.372
that turns every

00:00:08.184 --> 00:00:09.528
BAML program into

00:00:09.339 --> 00:00:10.483
native Rust code

00:00:11.014 --> 00:00:11.945
On average the

00:00:11.757 --> 00:00:13.101
compiled code runs

00:00:12.913 --> 00:00:14.080
about three and

00:00:13.891 --> 00:00:14.740
a half times

00:00:14.552 --> 00:00:15.388
faster than their

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.037
interpreter

00:00:16.191 --> 00:00:16.886
and up to

00:00:16.698 --> 00:00:18.242
thirty-four times faster

00:00:18.054 --> 00:00:19.056
on tight loops

00:00:19.574 --> 00:00:20.670
BAML reads like

00:00:20.482 --> 00:00:21.283
TypeScript

00:00:21.331 --> 00:00:22.380
is concurrent like

00:00:22.192 --> 00:00:22.710
Go

00:00:22.817 --> 00:00:23.972
has no async

00:00:23.784 --> 00:00:25.493
keyword and profiles

00:00:25.364 --> 00:00:26.578
every function call

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.026
down to the

00:00:26.838 --> 00:00:27.769
nanosecond

00:00:28.302 --> 00:00:29.316
Full story on

00:00:29.127 --> 00:00:30.023
the dashboard
